,"rotY":-0.2,"eyebrow":"Life support","title":"Oxygen out of thin air","body":"Martian air is 95% carbon dioxide. Split CO₂ and you get carbon and the O₂ you breathe. NASA really did this on Mars in 2021, with an instrument the size of a toaster."}},{"id":"1374a60c-3eb9-4851-ab91-7f700a14907e","createdAt":1786942186308,"transform":{"position":[11,3.552713678800501e-15,-16],"rotation":[0,-1,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"x":11,"z":-16,"rotY":-1,"eyebrow":"Crew quarters","title":"A day and a bit","body":"A Martian day — a \"sol\" — is 24 hours 37 minutes. Close enough to sleep by, but the extra 37 minutes add up: crews drift a whole night out of step with Earth in about a month."}},{"id":"78c6b93f-7351-465b-bbbd-6497c452aab0","createdAt":1786942186309,"transform":{"position":[-7,-6.661338147750939e-16,3],"rotation":[0,0.3,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"x":-7,"z":3,"rotY":0.3,"eyebrow":"Why the dome","title":"The air is the problem","body":"Outside, the pressure is under 1% of Earth's — so low that the water in your blood would boil. The dome is not for warmth. It is holding an atmosphere in."}},{"id":"43987b80-dc56-49fe-8a4c-9b9c01ab61e5","createdAt":1786942186310,"transform":{"position":[0,9.000000000000004,-14],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#f2a541"},{"id":"494f8852-6f70-4f2a-8ecd-30386b9f2ec9","createdAt":1786942186311,"transform":{"position":[-12,9.000000000000004,-20],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#e0455f"},{"id":"500e9c7f-f8fa-457a-8552-ad527b8541ef","createdAt":1786942186313,"transform":{"position":[12,9.000000000000004,-18],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#f2a541"},{"id":"3e4eb71e-ac3c-42d1-a991-2080819d9ab7","createdAt":1786942186314,"transform":{"position":[2,9.000000000000007,-28],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#f5f5f5"},{"id":"354d5499-6d9